guide forever/alliance/30-40/04b-stranglethorn-vale
title Stranglethorn Vale
faction Alliance
levels 35-36
zone Stranglethorn Vale
next forever/alliance/30-40/05-arathi-highlands
pitch For characters of 35 to 36, but several quests here are level 37-38: on purpose, for their experience. The water elementals are 36-37: pull them one at a time.

# Forge's route search orders the quests of this guide and its guide writer writes the steps.
# Fixes go into data/route-fixes.json, data/guide-fixes.json or forever-db/corrections, never
# into this file.
# Since 2026-11-07 Stranglethorn's second loop, after Desolace (the first loop is 30-40/04, which takes its Booty Bay
# quests). In from Duskwood at the north, down through the jungle, out at Booty Bay.
# Level tidy (0.4.0): the Lashtail Raptors (Raptor Mastery, 195) are hunted here at about 36 instead of on the first loop at
# 33-34, where Hemet gives it (Nesingwary's camp on the way in takes it for whoever didn't). Sin'Dall (Tiger Mastery, 188,
# level 37) waits for 40-50/01-stranglethorn-vale at about 41 (fix round 2: players reach this hill at about 35.5).
# Panther Mastery's Shadowmaw Panthers (192, 37-38) and Troll Witchery's Skullsplitter trolls (205, 39-42)
# are three and four levels over players here: 40-50/01-stranglethorn-vale works both at about 41. Brother Nimetz gives
# Troll Witchery here, when Kurzen's Mystery is handed in, and it is carried to that guide. Wendel Mathers'
# Cook in the Cage (97047) is taken at his cage here and worked on 40-50/01's Rebel Camp stop at about 41: its key drops
# only from the Subchiefs (35-36, three of them beside Colonel Kurzen, a 39-40 elite) and Elites (36-37), two over
# players here (fix round 1, 0.4.0). Zimmix Sputterspark (97329, 97331), Kebok's ears (189) and the Stolen Shipments
# (97328) from the first loop are worked in the ruins of Zul'Kunda here, beside the third tablet.
# Route review 0.4.3: Hostile Takeover (213) left this loop for 40-50/01-stranglethorn-vale (Kebok gives it there at about
# 41): Venture Co. Agents (39) walk among Lake Nazferiti's Geologists, three over players here at about 35.7.

step Collin Mauren
  when complete 1078
  zone Stormwind City
  turnin 1078                         -- In the Slaughtered Lamb, if you still carry it

step Fly to Darkshire
  zone Stormwind City
  goto 66.3,62.7 "Stormwind flight master"
  fly "Darkshire"
  zone Duskwood

step Stranglethorn Vale
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  goto 40.8,4.2 "Into Stranglethorn Vale"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The Rebel Camp

step Rebel Camp
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip From Duskwood take the road south; the camp sits in the hills west of the road.
  accept 207                          -- Brother Nimetz
  accept 574                          -- Sergeant Yohwa
  accept 210                          -- Corporal Kaleb, if 30-40/04 didn't give it: for Krazek in Booty Bay

step Nesingwary's Expedition
  tip South along the road: the hunters' tents stand just west of it. Ajeck and Hemet gave you these on the first loop: take them now only if you didn't.
  accept 188                          -- Ajeck Rouack, if 30-40/04 didn't give it: Sin'Dall, in the 40-50 Stranglethorn guide
  accept 195                          -- Hemet Nesingwary, if 30-40/04 didn't give it: the Lashtail Raptors, after the jungle ruins

step Bookie Herod
  when onquest 200
  tip East to Kurzen's Compound: Herod's records lie in a hut on its west side.
  turnin 200                          -- Bookie Herod's Records, upstairs
  accept 328

step Kurzen's Compound
  tip Wendel Mathers, a cook, is caged at the compound's western edge: take his quest now and keep it, his cage key and the fighter's uniform come on the 40-50 Stranglethorn guide, when the Subchiefs and Elites are your level. Headshrinkers stand deeper in the compound; the Commandos lurk stealthed around it and in the cave, and Herod's strongbox sits by the cave mouth. Pick up Green Hills pages as they drop.
  tip Careful: Kurzen Commandos are level 34-35, not elite, and often spawn stealthed; near death they use Smoke Bomb. Colonel Kurzen, an elite of 39-40, stands at the compound's north end: leave him be.
  accept 97047 @44.3,7.9 map 1434     -- Wendel Mathers, in his cage
  kill 938 quest 574.1 @46.3,7.8 map 1434 -- Kurzen Commando
  kill 941 quest 574.2 @46.4,7.9 map 1434 -- Kurzen Headshrinker, below ground
  turnin 328                          -- Bookie Herod's Strongbox, below ground
  accept 329

step The jungle ruins
  tip West across the jungle to the troll ruins: each holds one stone tablet of the troll legends, the first two in the ruins south-west of Nesingwary's camp, the last two on the hill in the north-west.
  tip Careful: the Saltscale murlocs on the shore near the second tablet are elite (35-37): swim to the tablet from the water and keep clear of them.
  collect 2005 quest 207.1            -- The First Troll Legend: Moon Over the Vale
  collect 2006 quest 207.2            -- The Second Troll Legend: Gri'lek the Wanderer; underwater

step Water Elementals
  tip The haunted island lies just off the shore west of the second tablet: the Lesser Water Elementals rise from the water around it.
  collect 3923 quest 601              -- Water Elemental Bracers

step The Ruins of Zul'Kunda
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip North along the coast to the ruins on the hill: the last two tablets lie there. Zimmix Sputterspark, a goblin, is caged beside the third tablet: any Bloodscalp can drop his Primitive Key, then lead him out of the ruins. The Stolen Shipments lie at the ruins' east edge. Pick up Green Hills pages as they drop.
  tip Careful: the Bloodscalp Berserkers, Headhunters and Witch Doctors (36-37) hold the ruins' core: pull them one at a time.
  collect 2007 quest 207.3            -- The Third Troll Legend: Fall of Gurubashi
  accept 97329                        -- Zimmix Sputterspark, in his cage beside the third tablet
  collect 1519 quest 189              -- Bloodscalp Ear
  collect 277957 quest 97329          -- Primitive Key, from the Bloodscalp trolls
  turnin 97329
  accept 97331                        -- For Wharfmaster Lozgil in Booty Bay, at the end of this loop
  complete 97331 @26.8,11.4
  collect 277953 quest 97328 @24.8,13.0 map 1434 -- Stolen Shipment
  collect 2008 quest 207.4            -- The Fourth Troll Legend: The Emperor's Tomb
  complete 339 optional               -- Chapter I
  complete 340 optional               -- Chapter II
  complete 341 optional               -- Chapter III
  complete 342 optional               -- Chapter IV

step The Lashtail raptors
  tip East from the ruins to the hilltop south-west of Nesingwary's camp: the Lashtail Raptors run in the jungle around it. Leave Sin'Dall, the great tiger (37) on the hilltop, to the 40-50 Stranglethorn guide: you're about 35 here. Then on to the hunters' tents.
  kill 686 quest 195                  -- Lashtail Raptor

step Nesingwary's Expedition
  turnin 339 optional                 -- Barnil Stonepot
  turnin 340 optional
  turnin 341 optional
  turnin 342 optional
  turnin 338 optional
  turnin 195                          -- Hemet Nesingwary
  accept 196                          -- Hemet Nesingwary: the Jungle Stalkers come in 40-50

step Rebel Camp
  tip North-east up the road to the Rebel Camp, then back south through the jungle.
  turnin 329                          -- Lieutenant Doren
  accept 330
  turnin 330                          -- Corporal Sethman
  accept 331
  turnin 331                          -- Lieutenant Doren
  turnin 574                          -- Sergeant Yohwa: the Commandos and Headshrinkers fell in the compound
  turnin 207                          -- Brother Nimetz
  accept 205                          -- keep it: the Skullsplitter Witch Doctors (41-42) wait for the 40-50 Stranglethorn guide

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- South

step Snapjaw Crocolisks
  tip Snapjaw Crocolisks bask along the river in the middle of the jungle, on the way south to Booty Bay.
  collect 4104 quest 577              -- Snapjaw Crocolisk Skin

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Booty Bay

step Booty Bay
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  turnin 577                          -- Drizzlik, inside
  turnin 601                          -- Baron Revilgaz, upstairs in the tavern
  accept 602                          -- For Archmage Ansirem in Alterac Mountains
  turnin 189                          -- Kebok, upstairs
  turnin 210                          -- Krazek, upstairs
  accept 627 optional -- Krazek, upstairs: this optional quest needs four Lesser Bloodstone Ore. Mine Lesser Bloodstone Deposits in Arathi Highlands with Mining 75, or buy the ore at the Auction House or ask a miner friend. The kobolds do not drop it; skip this quest if you cannot get the ore.
  accept 600                          -- Crank Fizzlebub, inside
  accept 606                          -- "Sea Wolf" MacKinley, on the top floor
  turnin 97331                        -- Wharfmaster Lozgil, on the docks
  turnin 97328                        -- Wharfmaster Lozgil
